# To-Do Webapp Implementation Plan

Create a premium, modern to-do list web application using Vanilla HTML, CSS, and JS. Now adding deadline support.

## Proposed Changes

### [Web App]
Create a responsive and visually stunning single-page application.

#### [NEW] [index.html](file:///c:/Users/HoMeW/Desktop/todo/index.html)
- Semantic HTML5 structure.
- SEO meta tags.
- Responsive design.
- Added date input for deadlines.

#### [NEW] [style.css](file:///c:/Users/HoMeW/Desktop/todo/style.css)
- Modern typography (Inter font).
- Dark mode by default with glassmorphism effects.
- Smooth transitions and hover animations.
- Custom scrollbar and premium color palette (HSL).
- Styled deadline tags and input.

#### [NEW] [script.js](file:///c:/Users/HoMeW/Desktop/todo/script.js)
- Core logic: Add, Delete, Toggle Completion.
- Persistence using `localStorage`.
- Animations for adding/removing items.
- Deadline handling and display formatting.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- N/A (Manual verification via browser).

### Manual Verification
1. Open [index.html](file:///c:/Users/HoMeW/Desktop/todo/index.html) in the browser.
2. Add a few tasks.
3. Mark tasks as complete.
4. Delete a task.
5. Refresh the page to verify persistence.
6. Verify responsive layout on different screen sizes.
7. Add a task with a deadline and verify display.
8. Verify tasks without deadlines still display correctly.
